        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-license" data-main="software" data-sub="license">
            <h3>License keys (installed program &rarr; where its license is stored)</h3>
            <div class="setgrid">
                <label for="setLicCollect">Collect software license keys (opt-in)</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setLicCollect">
                    <div class="hint">Master switch for the License keys section below. Off by default; nothing reads
                    licenses until you turn it on AND press Collect - or set an automatic interval below.</div></div>

                <label for="setLicInterval">Collect licenses automatically every (hours)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setLicInterval" class="num">
                    <select id="setLicIntervalSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">0 = off (on demand only, the default). Otherwise the server runs the same
                    read-only collection on every ONLINE Windows device on this cycle - 24 = daily, 168 = weekly.
                    Offline devices are skipped and keep their last result. The run never writes to a device, never
                    reboots it, and the keys stay on this server (they are never logged and never sent anywhere by
                    this feature). Devices that are busy with another task are skipped for that cycle.</div></div>

                <label for="setLicMsKeys">Include Microsoft product keys</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setLicMsKeys">
                    <div class="hint">Also read the Microsoft partial product key(s) from the WMI SoftwareLicensingProduct class on each Windows device.</div></div>
                <label for="setLicTableEnabled">Update license mapping table from repository</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setLicTableEnabled">
                    <select id="setLicTableEnabledSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">Curated table shipped in <code>license-table.json</code> and refreshed from its URL with the NVD cycle. Off: only your custom rules apply.</div></div>
                <label for="setLicTableUrl">License table URL</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setLicTableUrl" style="width:420px">
                    <select id="setLicTableUrlSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">https only; the rule table that maps a program name to where its license is stored.</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="info">
                For asset management the software-inventory CSV can also carry a <strong>License</strong> and
                <strong>License Source</strong> column. Like the CPE table, a rule table maps an installed program
                name to one or more <strong>extraction rules</strong>: a Windows registry value, a file read (with an
                optional regex whose group 1 is the key, a JSON field, or a line number), or a WMI class property.
                Rows labelled <em>Table</em> come from the curated <code>license-table.json</code> (refreshed from its
                URL); <em>Custom</em> rows are yours and win. Microsoft keys come from the <em>Include Microsoft
                product keys</em> switch above, not from a rule.<br>
                Reading runs as SYSTEM and is <strong>read-only</strong> (registry values / files / WMI properties
                only); the result is stored on this server under the device's data folder - nothing is sent anywhere
                and no key is ever written to a log. Turn on <em>Collect software license keys</em> above, then either
                press <em>Collect</em> or set an automatic interval above (0 = off, on demand only - the default).
                The CSV export (Software type) then includes the found keys; its <em>License Source</em> column names
                the rule type and, for per-user reads, the user (e.g. <code>registry (user: alice)</code>).
                <br><br>
                <strong>Per user and wildcards (v5.5.0):</strong> a rule can carry <code>"perUser": true</code>. On a
                registry rule the path is then written as <code>HKCU:\Software\...</code> and read from every
                <strong>already-loaded</strong> user hive (<code>HKEY_USERS\&lt;SID&gt;</code>) - hives of users who are
                not logged on are <strong>never loaded</strong>, the extraction stays strictly read-only. On a file
                rule the placeholder <code>\{{profile}}</code> in the path becomes each user's profile directory (e.g.
                <code>\{{profile}}\AppData\Roaming\Product\key.lic</code>). One single <code>*</code> is allowed per
                path: in a registry path it is one whole subkey segment that gets enumerated (version-dependent
                subkeys such as <code>License.ws.*</code>, at most 20 matches, first non-empty value wins), in a file
                path it is a leaf pattern (at most 5 candidate files). At most 20 user profiles are considered per run.
                <br><br>
                <strong>Microsoft licenses: type and activation state (v5.6.0):</strong> the <em>Include Microsoft
                product keys</em> switch reads the <code>SoftwareLicensingProduct</code> WMI class, which carries far
                more than the key. Besides the last five characters of the key the collection now stores the
                <strong>edition</strong> (<code>LicenseFamily</code>, e.g. <code>Office19Professional2019R_OEM_Perp</code>),
                the <strong>key channel</strong> (<code>Retail</code>, <code>OEM:DM</code>, <code>OEM:NONSLP</code>,
                <code>Volume:MAK</code>, <code>Volume:KMSCLIENT</code>, &hellip; - that is the license TYPE of the
                installation), the <strong>activation state</strong> (<code>LicenseStatus</code>: licensed,
                out-of-box/out-of-tolerance/extended grace, non-genuine grace, notification mode, unlicensed) and an
                evaluation end date. The <strong>Device list</strong> counts the licenses that are not activated per
                device and its <em>Details</em> button lists edition, channel and state. Still strictly read-only: one
                <code>Get-CimInstance</code>, no <code>slmgr</code> call, no activation change, and the full product key
                is never read - a <code>DigitalProductId</code> decode and the firmware
                <code>OA3xOriginalProductKey</code> are deliberately not used, because a full key is a usable secret
                and decoding it is what the AV-flagged key-finder tools do.
                <br><br>
                <strong>License type of a product</strong> (independent of any device) is curated in the mapping table:
                Vulnerabilities &rsaquo; CPE table carries a <em>License type</em> per row - an SPDX identifier
                (<code>MIT</code>, <code>GPL-2.0-only</code>, &hellip;) or <code>Proprietary</code> /
                <code>Freeware</code> / <code>Freeware (non-commercial)</code>. It appears as the <em>License Type</em>
                column of the software CSV and of the software list without any collection run. Seats, expiry and
                purchase data are not on a device at all - they belong to the asset-management system
                (Settings &rsaquo; Asset management).
                <br><br>
                <strong>Rules JSON</strong> example:
                <code>[{"type":"registry","path":"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Vendor\\App","value":"LicenseKey"}]</code>
                &middot; file: <code>[{"type":"file","path":"C:\\ProgramData\\App\\lic.dat","regex":"KEY=([A-Z0-9-]+)"}]</code>
                &middot; WMI: <code>[{"type":"wmi","class":"SoftwareLicensingProduct","property":"PartialProductKey","filter":"LicenseStatus=1"}]</code>
                &middot; per user: <code>[{"type":"registry","path":"HKCU:\\Software\\Vendor","value":"Serial","perUser":true}]</code>
            </div>
            <div class="hint" id="licTableSourceInfo"></div>
            <div class="controls">
                <button id="licCollectAllBtn" class="purple" data-help="lic.collectall">Collect licenses (all online Windows)</button>
                <span id="licRunInfo" class="hint"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="hint">Per device: the <strong>Device list</strong> shows how many keys were collected on each
            machine and how many Microsoft licenses are <strong>not activated</strong>, collects for the devices you
            tick there, and its <em>Details</em> button offers the collection for that single device plus the edition,
            key channel and activation state of every Microsoft license. The collected key values themselves are never
            displayed - they stay in
            <code>data/&lt;node&gt;/license.json</code> on this server and appear only in the software CSV export.</div>
            <h4 style="font-size:13px;color:#0b3d6b;margin:14px 0 6px 0;">Custom rules (you can add your own)</h4>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th style="cursor:default">Regex (display name)</th><th style="cursor:default">Label</th><th style="cursor:default">Rules</th><th style="width:120px;"></th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="licCustomBody"><tr><td colspan="4" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
            </table></div>
            <div class="controls">
                <input id="licMatch" type="text" placeholder="Regex, e.g. ^Adobe Illustrator" style="min-width:200px;">
                <input id="licLabel" type="text" placeholder="Label, e.g. Adobe Illustrator CC" style="min-width:160px;">
                <input id="licRules" type="text" placeholder='Rules JSON, e.g. [{"type":"registry","path":"HKLM:\\...","value":"LicenseKey"}]' style="min-width:360px;">
                <button id="addLicBtn" data-help="lic.add">Add</button>
            </div>
            <div class="controls">
                <label style="font-weight:400;" data-help="lic.peruser"><input type="checkbox" id="licPerUser"> apply these rules per user
                (registry paths as HKCU:, file paths may use the profile placeholder, one * wildcard per path allowed)</label>
            </div>
            <div id="licMsg"></div>
            <h4 style="font-size:13px;color:#0b3d6b;margin:14px 0 6px 0;">License collection log</h4>
            <div><button id="refreshLicLogBtn" class="small" data-help="lic.refreshlog">Refresh log</button> <span id="licLogInfo" class="hint"></span></div>
            <pre id="licLog" style="max-height:200px;overflow:auto;background:#0f1720;color:#cfe3f5;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11px;margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;">(not loaded yet)</pre>
            <div class="controls" style="margin-top:16px;"><button id="saveSettingsBtn3" data-help="set.save">Save license settings</button></div>
            <div id="licenseMsg"></div>
        </div>
